menu "XPRS station storage"

config SDCARD_MAX_FILES
    int "How many files may be open on the card at once"
    default 5
    range 2 10
    help
        With CONFIG_FATFS_SECTOR_4096 and CONFIG_FATFS_PER_FILE_CACHE --
        which both boards use -- every open FILE holds a 4 KB sector cache,
        so this number costs four kilobytes of heap each and is one of the
        largest single allocations either board makes.

        Five is right for the M5Stack, whose store keeps three files open
        while a query opens two more. The T-Dongle keeps the index segment
        and the store-and-forward spool open and reads one at a time, so
        three fits it and hands eight kilobytes back to a heap that has
        none to spare. docs/esp32.md records what happened the last time
        this number was raised "to be safe".
endmenu
